Log_Domain_Status amber fix — live Excel probe transcript
==========================================================

Root cause: the amber half of Log_Domain_Status sums the materialized
sample-include reader with N():
    d = SUMPRODUCT(N(base)) - SUMPRODUCT(N(Fit_Sample_Include()))
N() of a range-returning thunk (the Fit_Sample_Include() reader, whether
spelled `#`/ANCHORARRAY or OFFSET) collapses to the top-left cell (=1),
so the buggy term returns 1 and d = (complete cases) - 1 = n-1, firing a
false "n-1 rows excluded: Log of <= 0" amber on EVERY sheet regardless of
transforms. On a real Log (drop <= 0) sheet that n-1 false amber ALSO masks
the genuine, intended excluded-row count.

Fix: sum the reader with `--` instead of N():
    d = SUMPRODUCT(N(base)) - SUMPRODUCT(--(Fit_Sample_Include()))
`--` coerces a range OR an array to a summable 1/0 array, so it is robust
to the reader's form and to Sample_Include()'s promotion to the reader.

These probes do NOT rebuild the shipped dist (it is stale for unrelated
v3.9 categorical reasons; rebuilding it is a separate PR). They evaluate
the exact buggy and fixed amber bodies against the REAL reader on each
sheet by writing the amber-half LET into scratch cells and reading the
verdict under CalculateFull (normal recalc -- the regime where the symptom
fires; CalculateFullRebuild hides it, which is why verify-models never
reproduced the amber).

(ASCII: "? 0" in the verdict strings is the "<= 0" glyph, replaced by the
ascii-safe probe helper.)

